      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mattapan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Native Americans first inhabited the area that became Mattapan, long before European settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mattapan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1848, a cemetery was founded in Mattapan to provide a park‑like setting for burials and remembrance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mattapan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The neighborhood was annexed by Boston in 1870, spurring growth as streetcars and railroads linked it to downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bostonplans.org/neighborhoods/mattapan/at-a-glance"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mattapan’s Red Line station, the last stop on the line, opened in 1981 and remains a key transit hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
